WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.523
Welcome to the Mosaic Signal course,

00:00:02.523 --> 00:00:06.869
one of the three courses toward
Mosaic Practitioner Certified.

00:00:06.869 --> 00:00:12.196
You already know how Mosaic Signal, one
of the Mosaic tools developed by Dr.

00:00:12.196 --> 00:00:13.878
Chris Cancialosi, works.

00:00:13.878 --> 00:00:18.434
This course makes you the person
a client trusts to run one well,

00:00:18.434 --> 00:00:21.448
from the first conversation
to the readout.

00:00:21.448 --> 00:00:26.776
It takes about four hours, including a
written practical and the final exam.

00:00:27.267 --> 00:00:30.496
A practitioner can run
a Mosaic Signal survey.

00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:33.656
This course is about
making it worth running.

00:00:33.656 --> 00:00:39.202
You'll learn to frame a study so the
stories answer the client's real question.

00:00:39.202 --> 00:00:43.765
To design questions about the
story that produce honest patterns.

00:00:43.765 --> 00:00:48.188
To field the survey without
breaking a promise to a respondent.

00:00:48.188 --> 00:00:52.752
To read the results the way an
expert does: shape before average,

00:00:52.752 --> 00:00:55.911
stories before claims,
and outliers as clues.

00:00:55.911 --> 00:01:01.177
Then to compare waves, work inside
Culture Dig, and present what you found.

00:01:01.177 --> 00:01:04.125
And you'll prove it with an analysis memo.

00:01:04.633 --> 00:01:10.394
You met the basics in the Mosaic Practitioner
course: people tell a story and then

00:01:10.394 --> 00:01:15.381
interpret their own story, the four
question types, the four templates,

00:01:15.381 --> 00:01:20.158
the one-launch rules, and the habit
of reading shape before average.

00:01:20.158 --> 00:01:22.125
We won't repeat any of that.

00:01:22.125 --> 00:01:27.745
Instead, each module goes a level deeper:
what the respondent cap really counts,

00:01:27.745 --> 00:01:33.084
what every chart hides, and why even
Culture Dig's score can be fooled by an

00:01:33.084 --> 00:01:33.646
average.

00:01:33.646 --> 00:01:38.984
If any of the basics feel hazy, revisit
Module 6 of the Mosaic course first.

00:01:39.500 --> 00:01:41.335
There are seven modules.

00:01:41.335 --> 00:01:46.916
After this orientation come framing,
question design, fielding, analysis,

00:01:46.916 --> 00:01:49.210
and then waves and presenting.

00:01:49.210 --> 00:01:51.810
The last module is your practical.

00:01:51.810 --> 00:01:55.786
You'll pass a short check
at the end of each module,

00:01:55.786 --> 00:02:01.596
with eighty percent and unlimited retakes,
and a thirty-question final exam,

00:02:01.596 --> 00:02:03.355
also at eighty percent.

00:02:03.355 --> 00:02:08.095
Three of its questions protect
rules that can never be broken,

00:02:08.095 --> 00:02:11.689
so getting any of them
wrong fails the attempt.

00:02:11.689 --> 00:02:14.671
Passing the exam completes this course.

00:02:14.671 --> 00:02:18.494
Your two-page analysis
memo, scored with a rubric,

00:02:18.494 --> 00:02:22.393
is task three of your Mosaic
Practitioner capstone.

00:02:22.900 --> 00:02:25.487
Let's catch up with Northwind Health.

00:02:25.487 --> 00:02:28.563
After the merger with
Lakeside Clinic Group,

00:02:28.563 --> 00:02:31.500
their Culture Mosaic showed Collaboration,

00:02:31.500 --> 00:02:35.205
Change Ready and Empowered
Teams as the lowest tiles.

00:02:35.205 --> 00:02:39.960
Their first Mosaic Signal collected
a hundred and forty-two stories,

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:44.155
and the message was clear: staff
were willing, but not able.

00:02:44.155 --> 00:02:46.951
By October, collaboration was improving,

00:02:46.951 --> 00:02:50.377
but decisions still felt
closed to the frontline.

00:02:50.377 --> 00:02:55.621
In this course you'll look deeper at
that first study, see its second wave,

00:02:55.621 --> 00:02:58.837
help design a new study
on how decisions land,

00:02:58.837 --> 00:03:01.564
and then analyze it for your practical.

00:03:01.564 --> 00:03:03.452
You'll meet two new people.

00:03:03.452 --> 00:03:07.577
Jamie Ortiz is Northwind's
organizational development lead,

00:03:07.577 --> 00:03:11.912
who runs the surveys and writes
the first draft of everything.

00:03:11.912 --> 00:03:14.988
Morgan Ellis is a Mosaic
framework designer.

00:03:14.988 --> 00:03:17.365
Alex Moreau is still your sponsor.

00:03:17.867 --> 00:03:19.828
Three tips before you start.

00:03:19.828 --> 00:03:24.873
Use the shared training workspace:
Mosaic Signal surveys there are free,

00:03:24.873 --> 00:03:30.337
with no respondent limit and no deadline,
so you can build and test as you go.

00:03:30.337 --> 00:03:33.700
Product details are current
as of November 2026,

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:38.674
so if a screen disagrees with the
course, trust the screen and tell us.

00:03:38.674 --> 00:03:40.636
And keep the case file open.

00:03:40.636 --> 00:03:45.400
It holds every Northwind number,
including your practical's dataset.
